WEBVTT

0
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:06.300
Sprezzature is an AI engine for Design.
Audio reads speech both ways.

1
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.780
A recording becomes timed text.
Written text becomes timed speech.

2
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.075
Your video has captions
and they are accurate.

3
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.440
90 characters on screen,
for half a second. Nobody reads that.

4
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.325
Turn it around. A page reads aloud,
and highlights the wrong line.

5
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:33.975
One modality, read in both directions,
and never leaving your machine.

6
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.400
Sound into text: what was said,
who said it, in which language.

7
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.440
Text into sound: a WAV,
and a WebVTT beside it.

8
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:50.239
The same timed track either way.
That is how a page follows a reading.

9
00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.800
These are not numbers somebody liked.
They have a publisher.

10
00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:03.160
Netflix's timed text style guide,
and the code says so in a comment.

11
00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:09.680
17 characters a second.
42 to a line. 2 lines at most.

12
00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.037
Conventions, not laws,
which is why each one is a dial.

13
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.937
Here is the whole package on one page.
Follow either lane down.

14
00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.920
They do not stay apart.
Both arrive at the same gate.

15
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:37.600
A narration and a transcript are one file,
so one reader checks both.

16
00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:46.720
Go to sprezzature.ai,
and drop a GitHub star if it deserves it.

17
00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.280
Make it, audit it, take a look at it.
